{"id":"st2047-2","designation":"ST 2047-2","title":"Carriage of VC-2 Compressed Video — Carriage of VC-2 CompressedVideo over HD-SDI","state":"active","suite":"2047","official":{"family_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/doc/st2047-2/","latest_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/latest/st2047-2/","checked_at":"2026-11-18"},"scope":"This standard defines a means of mapping VC-2 data onto a single HD SDI link, based upon the SMPTE 292 data structure, to support the transport of 1920 x 1080/50/P, 1920 x 1080/59.94/P (60/1.001), and 1920 x 1080/60/P systems with 4:2:2 Y’C’BC’R color encoding. As these systems require a raw uncompressed data capacity twice that of SMPTE 292, VC-2 mezzanine compression as defined by SMPTE RP 2047-1 is required to reduce the data rate. This link supports the carriage of embedded audio, ancillary data and payload identification. A signal coded in accordance with this standard incorporates a noisy but recognizable picture that can be viewed using a standard SMPTE 292 video monitor.","outline":[{"level":1,"title":"SMPTE Standard","page":1},{"level":1,"title":"Carriage of VC-2 Compressed","page":1},{"level":1,"title":"Video over HD-SDI","page":1},{"level":1,"title":"Page 1 of 11 pages","page":1},{"level":1,"title":"Table of Contents Page","page":1},{"level":1,"title":"Foreword","page":2},{"level":1,"title":"Intellectual Property","page":2},{"level":1,"title":"Introduction","page":2},{"level":1,"title":"Scope","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"Conformance Notation","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"Normative References","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"General Description","page":4},{"level":2,"title":"Source Image Formats","page":4},{"level":2,"title":"Timing Reference Codes","page":4},{"level":2,"title":"Ancillary Data","page":4},{"level":2,"title":"Audio Data","page":4},{"level":2,"title":"Time Code","page":4},{"level":2,"title":"Video Payload Identifier","page":4},{"level":2,"title":"Viewable Content","page":6},{"level":1,"title":"VC-2 Mezzanine Bit-stream Mapping",